  "independentArtReview": "Reviewed the attached 3×3 contact sheet.\n\n**Grade (style only): CONDITIONAL PASS**\n\nNew mobile clearly shares desktop's realistic scene language — textured buildings, stone wall, realistic rifle and hands, sky and sun, organic trees, soldier actor. It is far removed from the old blockout.\n\nRemaining differences:\n- **Water:** the biggest gap. Desktop has dark, reflective, rippled water; new mobile reads as pale, milky, flat sheets with little reflection. In the bank row it looks almost like sand.\n- **Soil:** mobile is more uniformly orange-tan and flatter, with less wet/dry variation and weaker shoreline blending.\n- **Foliage:** mobile canopies are darker and denser, lacking desktop's lighter, airy green; the grove's green grass looks largely missing.\n- **Lighting:** slightly flatter contrast and fewer specular highlights.",
